    "title": "Lepton-Flavor-Dependent Angular Analysis of $B\\\\to K^* \\\\ell^+ \\\\ell^-$ Decays at Belle",
    "arxiv": "[1612.05014v1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1612.05014)",
    "time": "2016.12.15",
    "abstract": "We present a lepton-flavor-dependent angular analysis of the rare decay $B \\\\to K^* \\\\ell^+ \\\\ell^-$, where $\\\\ell = e, \\\\mu$. The analysis is based on a data sample of 772 million $B\\\\bar{B}$ pairs collected at the $\\\\Upsilon(4S)$ resonance with the Belle detector. We measure the angular observables $P_4'$ and $P_5'$ as a function of the dilepton invariant mass squared $q^2$, as well as the lepton-flavor-universality-violating observables $Q_4$ and $Q_5$. All results are consistent with Standard Model predictions.",
